# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Blackcat Informatics® Inc. <paudley@blackcatinformatics.ca>
# SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0
#
# The work-orchestration core slice: the DOMAIN BINDING of the general
# prescription/enactment/commitment kernel.
#
# The kernel lives in `logic:` and is declared standalone - it takes no axiom
# edge into `gmeow:` - so one algebra serves a workflow, a DAG, a repeatable
# guide, a curriculum, a control plan and an organizational guide alike. Every
# `gmeow:`-typed edge the durable-work reading needs lives HERE, and the bridge
# direction is always domain-specializes-kernel (gmeow:X logic:subPropertyOf
# logic:Y), never the reverse.
#
# It mints no second recommendation model, no second budget, no second frontier
# and no second authority gate: those exist in the kernel and in preference, and
# this slice reaches them.

@prefix gmeow:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix logic:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix math:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix lang:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/lang/> .

gmeow:WorkCluster
    a logic:Kind ,
        owl:Class ;
    logic:subClassOf gmeow:SocialObject ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "Work Cluster"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A CONTINUING body of work: a standing goal, the policy governing it, the recurrence that issues occurrences, the prescription version currently in force, the guidance that governs how it is done, and the working memory it has accumulated. It is the thing that persists between occurrences and is never itself enacted — enactments are what its recurrence generates. Typed APART from logic:Enactment, which is one occurrence, and from logic:Plan, which is the prescription: a cluster OWNS a prescription and outlives every version of it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:adrReview a gmeow:WorkCluster ; gmeow:clusterSchedule ex:weeklySchedule ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for work that continues indefinitely and recurs — a weekly review, a standing control loop, a rolling curriculum."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid for one-off work (that is a single enactment) and avoid treating the cluster as the thing that runs."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Bind the goal, the policy, the schedule, the active prescription version, the guidance set and the note set; occurrences arrive through the schedule."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

gmeow:clusterGoal
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkCluster ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:Goal ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "cluster goal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The continuing goal the cluster exists to serve. Where that goal is a maintenance goal, a successful occurrence never closes it — the goal is satisfied only while its condition holds, so the cluster keeps recurring by design rather than by oversight."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterGoal ex:decisionsStayReviewed ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to name the continuing goal a cluster exists to serve."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid binding a per-occurrence goal here: 'this week's review is done' is the enactment's success criterion, not the cluster's reason to exist."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Where the goal is a maintenance goal, expect it to stay open across successful occurrences — that is the design, not an unfinished state."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:clusterPolicy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkCluster ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:Norm ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "cluster policy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The norm governing how the cluster's work may be carried out — what requires approval, what is forbidden, who may decide. Non-functional: several norms may govern one cluster, and where they disagree the disagreement is data rather than an error to resolve by picking one."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterPolicy ex:reviewPolicy ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for the norm governing how the cluster's work is conducted — quorum, escalation, publication."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid conflating it with the approval policy on a specific dispatch; that one governs a single authorization, this one governs the cluster."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Bind the norm that a reviewer would cite when asking whether an occurrence was run properly."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:clusterSchedule
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkCluster ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:EventSchedule ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "cluster schedule"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The schedule that issues the cluster's occurrences, mediating the recurrence rule and the generated events. Reuses the calendar spine rather than minting a recurrence vocabulary: the schedule is the GENERATOR, and an enactment is generated by an occurrence rather than being one."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterSchedule ex:weeklyThursday ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to bind the schedule that generates the cluster's occurrences."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid encoding the recurrence inline; the calendar slice owns recurrence rules and re-minting one is a second source of truth."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "The schedule carries the template event and the recurrence rule; the occurrences it generates are what give rise to enactments."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:clusterOccurrenceSeries
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkCluster ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:EventSeries ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "cluster occurrence series"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The series of concrete occurrences the cluster's schedule has issued, reached through the events spine. Reused, never re-minted: the recurrence rule belongs to the series and a skipped occurrence is a schedule exception rather than a missing member."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterOccurrenceSeries ex:weeklyReviewSeries ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to reach the calendar series whose occurrences generate this cluster's enactments."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid identifying an occurrence with the enactment it gives rise to; a skipped occurrence is a schedule exception, not an enactment in some skipped state."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Resolve recurrence through the calendar vocabulary rather than minting a local rule — the schedule is the generator, not the generated."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:clusterActivePrescription
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkCluster ;
    rdfs:range logic:PrescriptionVersion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "cluster active prescription"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The prescription version new occurrences will be enacted against. Functional, and deliberately a POINTER: an enactment pins its version at start, so moving this pointer mid-flight revises what happens next without rewriting what is already running."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterActivePrescription ex:reviewProcessV4 ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to point a continuing cluster at the prescription version new occurrences should enact."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid reading it as the version a RUNNING enactment uses: an in-flight enactment pins its own version at start, and this pointer moves independently."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Move the pointer when the process is revised; enactments already running keep the version they pinned, which is what stops a mid-week change rewriting this week's work."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:clusterEnactment
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkCluster ;
    rdfs:range logic:Enactment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "cluster enactment"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "One occurrence the cluster has generated. Multi-valued and append-only: this is the cluster's history, and a prior occurrence stays readable and comparable after later ones begin."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterEnactment ex:weekTwelve , ex:weekThirteen ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to collect the occurrences a continuing cluster has produced, so history is reachable from the cluster."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid treating the set as ordered or complete-by-construction; occurrences are generated over time and a skipped one leaves no enactment at all."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Add one enactment per occurrence that actually ran; a schedule exception is recorded on the schedule, never as a missing member here."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:clusterNote
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkCluster ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:Note ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "cluster note"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A retained note the cluster carries between occurrences — its working memory. Multi-valued. Retention is the point: a cluster that forgets what the last occurrence learned is a schedule, not a continuing body of work."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterNote ex:deprecationBacklogNote ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for standing notes that outlive any single occurrence — the context a new occurrence should inherit."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid recording per-occurrence observations here; those belong to the enactment that made them, or they will resurface forever."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Keep the set small and current: a standing note nobody prunes becomes noise the next occurrence learns to skip."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:GuidanceSet
    a logic:Kind ,
        owl:Class ;
    logic:subClassOf gmeow:InformationObject ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "Guidance Set"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The versioned body of rubrics and checklists governing how a cluster's work is done. Versioned through the standard version-membership relator rather than a bespoke mechanism, because 'which guidance governed THAT occurrence' must stay answerable after the guidance has moved on — and an unversioned guidance set silently rewrites the past every time it is edited."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:adrGuidanceV2 a gmeow:GuidanceSet ; gmeow:guidanceRubric ex:adrRubric ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for the rubrics and checklists a recurring cluster applies, when past occurrences must remain judgeable by the guidance they actually ran under."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid editing a guidance set in place, and avoid attaching guidance directly to an occurrence without a version."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Bind rubrics and checklists; version it with a membership relator and record the governing version on each occurrence's context assembly."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

gmeow:clusterGuidanceSet
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkCluster ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:GuidanceSet ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "cluster guidance set"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The guidance currently governing the cluster. Functional, and a pointer like the active prescription: an occurrence records the version it actually ran under rather than inheriting whatever this later points at."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterGuidanceSet ex:reviewGuidance ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to attach the versioned rubrics and checklists a cluster's occurrences run under."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid attaching unversioned guidance: a decision made under one revision must not later be judged by another."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Pair with the context assembly's guidance-version binding so each occurrence records which revision actually governed it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:guidanceRubric
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:GuidanceSet ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:Rubric ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "guidance rubric"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A rubric the guidance set applies, reusing the norms rubric rather than minting a parallel assessment vocabulary. Multi-valued."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:reviewGuidance gmeow:guidanceRubric ex:adrQualityRubric ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for the rubric an occurrence is assessed against."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid changing a rubric in place mid-cycle; supersede it, or past assessments silently change meaning."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Bind the rubric the guidance version carried, so an assessment and its yardstick stay together."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:guidanceChecklist
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:GuidanceSet ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "guidance checklist"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A checklist the guidance set applies. Range an information object carrying the checklist content, whose textual surface grounds in the lang: form vocabulary. Multi-valued."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:reviewGuidance gmeow:guidanceChecklist ex:adrChecklist ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for the checklist an occurrence works through."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid treating the checklist as the plan; it governs how a step is done, not which steps exist."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Version it with the guidance set so a past occurrence remains judgeable by the checklist it actually used."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:guidanceVersionMembership
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:GuidanceSet ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:VersionMembership ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "guidance version membership"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint-scoped membership relator placing this guidance set in its version lineage. Reused rather than re-minted, so guidance versioning behaves exactly as every other versioned entity does."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:reviewGuidance gmeow:guidanceVersionMembership ex:guidanceV2 ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to place a guidance set in its version lineage."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid leaving it unbound: guidance with no version cannot be cited as the thing that governed a decision."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Reuse the shared version-membership vocabulary rather than minting a local revision counter."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:enactmentContextAssembly
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:Enactment ;
    rdfs:range logic:ContextAssembly ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "enactment context assembly"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The record of what was surfaced to this occurrence and what was withheld — the binding that makes 'which notes were surfaced to this run, under which guidance version' answerable. Functional: one assembly per occurrence, so the answer is unambiguous."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:weekThirteen gmeow:enactmentContextAssembly ex:week13Context ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to record what was actually put in front of the decider for this occurrence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid leaving it unbound on an enactment that produced decisions: without it, a later dissent cannot be weighed against what was visible at the time."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Exactly one assembly per enactment; it carries both what was included and what was withheld."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:preparationActivity
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    logic:subPropertyOf logic:preparationOf ;
    rdfs:domain logic:PreparationStep ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:Activity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "preparation activity"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The domain binding of the kernel's preparation seam onto the provenance activity spine: the concrete activity that carried out a preparation step. Specializes the kernel property rather than duplicating it, which is the direction every bridge in this slice runs."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:stageFiles gmeow:preparationActivity ex:ocrRun ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to record the activity that prepared an enactment or step for execution."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid recording preparation as though it were the prepared step; a preparation that ran does not mean the step it prepared for did."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Pair with a preparation receipt so the preparation is evidenced rather than asserted."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:frontierCandidateSet
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:ActionableFrontier ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:CandidateSet ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "frontier candidate set"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The frontier's candidate actions as a preference candidate set, so contextual comparison runs through the EXISTING preference apparatus instead of a second recommendation model. Functional. This is the binding that gives the frontier ties, incomparability and the no-global-winner discipline for free."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:remediationFrontier gmeow:frontierCandidateSet ex:remediationOptions ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to route the frontier's options through the existing preference apparatus."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid minting a local candidate list; a second recommendation model is a second source of truth about what the options are."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Bind the candidate set the comparison context ranks, so ties and incomparability are preserved rather than flattened."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:frontierComparisonContext
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:ActionableFrontier ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:ComparisonContext ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "frontier comparison context"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The context a frontier's recommendations are relative to. Functional. Recommendations without a context are the context-free global winner the preference apparatus exists to forbid, so this binding is what keeps a ranking honest."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:remediationFrontier gmeow:frontierComparisonContext ex:fastestRestore ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to make a frontier's recommendation explicitly relative to a policy."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid a context-free ranking: without a context there is no rule for what counts as better, and any winner is manufactured."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Two contexts over the same candidates may disagree, and both classifications coexist as attributed claims."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:entryHardFailure
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:FrontierEntry ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:VerifierVerdict ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "entry hard failure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The verifier verdict blocking a frontier entry, reusing preference's hard/soft constraint apparatus. A hard failure may not be traded away by a favourable score elsewhere, which is exactly the guarantee the reused vocabulary already enforces."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:ocrEntry gmeow:entryHardFailure ex:capabilityVerdict ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to bind a frontier entry to the hard-failure verdict that blocks it, reusing the preference apparatus rather than a local flag."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid inventing a boolean 'blocked' field; a hard failure carries a verdict and a reason, and a bare flag discards both."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Point at the verifier verdict so the block is explicable and can be re-evaluated when the condition changes."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:approvalGoverningNorm
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    logic:subPropertyOf logic:approvalPolicy ;
    rdfs:domain logic:ApprovalCommitment ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:Norm ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "approval governing norm"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The domain binding of the kernel's approval-policy seam onto the norms spine. Specializes the kernel property, so a commitment's policy is a real norm rather than an opaque reference."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:publishApproval gmeow:approvalGoverningNorm ex:publicationPolicy ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to name the policy under which an approval was granted, so a later reviewer can ask whether that policy still stands."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid leaving it unbound on a granted approval: an approval whose governing policy is unrecorded cannot be re-examined when the policy changes."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Bind exactly one norm per approval commitment; if two policies bear on the decision, the governing one is the one the approver acted under."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:ContributionKind
    a logic:AbstractIndividualType ,
        owl:Class ;
    logic:subClassOf logic:QualityValue ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "Contribution Kind"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Whether a recorded contribution came from a model, a human operator, or a tool. Closed and mandatory on every contribution, because the three carry different authority: a model contribution is advice, an operator contribution may be a decision, and a tool contribution is an observation. A review surface that cannot distinguish them cannot tell a reader who actually decided."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:draftComment gmeow:contributionKind gmeow:contributionModel ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use on every recorded contribution to a cluster or occurrence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid an unattributed contribution, and avoid inferring the kind from the content."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Attach exactly one member alongside the standard provenance attribution."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

gmeow:contributionModel a owl:NamedIndividual , gmeow:ContributionKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "model contribution"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Generated by a model. Always advice: it may inform a decision and may never be one, and it may never authorize an effect."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

gmeow:contributionOperator a owl:NamedIndividual , gmeow:ContributionKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "operator contribution"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Made by a human operator. The only kind that may carry a decision, and the kind an approval commitment names."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

gmeow:contributionTool a owl:NamedIndividual , gmeow:ContributionKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "tool contribution"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Produced by a deterministic tool. An observation rather than advice or decision: it reports what a tool found, and its authority is the tool's correctness."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

gmeow:contributionKind
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:ContributionKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "contribution kind"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a recorded contribution to its exactly-one kind. Domain a contribution record (stated in prose). Functional and mandatory."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:draftSummary gmeow:contributionKind gmeow:contributionModel ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use on every recorded contribution, so model output, operator judgement and tool output stay distinguishable."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid omitting it: an unattributed recommendation is indistinguishable from an authorized decision once it is a week old."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Bind exactly one of model, operator or tool — the value set is closed precisely so the distinction cannot blur."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:WorkReviewProjection
    a logic:Kind ,
        owl:Class ;
    logic:subClassOf gmeow:InformationObject ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "Work Review Projection"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The comprehensive operator view of a cluster, carrying all eight required contents: the continuing goal and its recurrence, the current prescription and its revision lineage, the current occurrence and its exact input generation, the derived frontier with recommendations and blockers, approvals and pending inputs, effect and reconciliation and compensation status, accumulated notes and decisions and artifacts and receipts and prior-occurrence comparison, and an exact accessible graph or timeline representation. It is a PROJECTION and says so: it necessarily collapses standpoint-indexed classifications into one readable surface, and that loss is disclosed on its receipt rather than hidden."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:w12Review a gmeow:WorkReviewProjection ; gmeow:reviewReceipt ex:w12Receipt ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to present a cluster's whole state to a human operator."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid treating it as canonical, and avoid shipping one without a preservation judgment."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Bind all eight contents and a projection receipt carrying exactly one preservation kind, with a named boundary for any non-exact kind."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

gmeow:reviewOfCluster
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkReviewProjection ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:WorkCluster ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "review of cluster"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a review projection to the cluster it presents. Functional."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewOfCluster ex:adrReviewCluster ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to bind a review projection to the continuing cluster it belongs to."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid a review with no cluster: an occurrence report detached from its cluster loses the history that makes it interpretable."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Exactly one cluster per review projection."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:reviewReceipt
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkReviewProjection ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:ProjectionReceipt ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "review receipt"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The projection receipt disclosing what this view preserved and what it dropped, reusing the shipped receipt vocabulary rather than minting a parallel one. Functional and MANDATORY: an operator view that collapses coexisting standpoints without saying so misrepresents disagreement as consensus."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewReceipt ex:projectionReceipt ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to attach the projection receipt recording what the review preserved and what it dropped."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid a receipt claiming exact preservation for a lossy projection; name the expressiveness boundary instead."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Bind exactly one preservation kind, and for any non-exact kind a named boundary."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:reviewGoalAndRecurrence
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkReviewProjection ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "review goal and recurrence"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Content one of eight: the continuing goal and the recurrence issuing occurrences. Range the goal-and-recurrence view (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewGoalAndRecurrence ex:goalSummary ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to state the continuing goal and the recurrence in the review projection."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid implying a maintenance goal was closed by a successful occurrence; it is satisfied only while its condition holds."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Show the schedule as well as the goal, so the next occurrence is predictable."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:reviewPrescriptionLineage
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkReviewProjection ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "review prescription lineage"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Content two of eight: the current prescription and how it was revised to get here. Range the lineage view (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewPrescriptionLineage ex:processLineage ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to show the current prescription and how it was revised."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid showing only the current version; the revision lineage is what explains why this occurrence differs from the last."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Follow supersession rather than mutation, so each prior version remains citable."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:reviewCurrentEnactment
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkReviewProjection ;
    rdfs:range logic:Enactment ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "review current enactment"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Content three of eight: the occurrence in progress and, through it, the exact input generation it pinned."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewCurrentEnactment ex:weekThirteen ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to bind the review projection to the occurrence it reports on."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid binding the cluster here; a review reports on one occurrence against one input snapshot."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Carry the exact input snapshot alongside, or the report cannot be reproduced."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:reviewFrontier
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkReviewProjection ;
    rdfs:range logic:ActionableFrontier ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "review frontier"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Content four of eight: the derived frontier with its recommendations and blockers."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewFrontier ex:week13Frontier ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to include the derived frontier, with recommendations and blockers, in the review projection."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid presenting a frontier without its saturation witness; an unwitnessed closure claim reads as complete when it may be cut."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Carry each entry's axis tuple so a reader can ask why an action carries the label it does."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:reviewApprovalsAndPending
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkReviewProjection ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "review approvals and pending inputs"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Content five of eight: outstanding authorizations and awaited inputs. Range the approvals view (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewApprovalsAndPending ex:pendingApprovals ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to surface what is awaiting a human in the review projection."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid listing only granted approvals; the pending ones are what an operator is being asked to act on."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Show the approval state, not just its existence, so an expired approval is distinguishable from a live one."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:reviewEffectStatus
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkReviewProjection ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "review effect status"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Content six of eight: effect, reconciliation and compensation status. Range the effect-status view (stated in prose). The content an operator needs most when something went wrong at the boundary."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewEffectStatus ex:sagaStatus ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to surface effect, reconciliation and compensation status in the review."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid reporting an undetermined outcome as a failure; undetermined and failed license different next actions."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Where an outcome is undetermined, say what is owed — reconciliation — rather than only that it is unknown."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:reviewAccumulatedRecord
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkReviewProjection ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "review accumulated record"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Content seven of eight: notes, decisions, artifacts, receipts and the comparison with prior occurrences. Range the accumulated-record view (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewAccumulatedRecord ex:decisionLog ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for the notes, decisions, artifacts and receipts a review projection carries forward."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid summarising the record in place of citing it; a summary cannot be re-examined."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Include the prior-occurrence comparison, which is what makes a continuing cluster's history useful rather than merely present."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:reviewTimelineRepresentation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:WorkReviewProjection ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "review timeline representation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Content eight of eight: an exact, accessible graph or timeline rendering. Range the timeline view (stated in prose); its textual surface grounds in the lang: rendering vocabulary."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewTimelineRepresentation ex:timelineGraph ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for the accessible graph or timeline rendering of the review."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid a rendering that carries claims the underlying record does not; a timeline is a projection, not a second source."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Ground the rendering surface so its accessibility commitments are explicit rather than assumed."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:FrontierExplanation
    a logic:Kind ,
        owl:Class ;
    logic:subClassOf gmeow:InformationObject ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "Frontier Explanation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Why one frontier entry carries the position it does, in the five terms an operator actually needs: the proof, the evidence, the governing policy, the cost/risk/benefit criteria, and the DISSENTING attributed observations. Dissent is a required content rather than a courtesy — an explanation that presents only the supporting view has told the operator what to think rather than what is known."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:ocrWhyBlocked a gmeow:FrontierExplanation ; gmeow:explanationDissent ex:reviewerObjection ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for every recommended or blocked action an operator may act on."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid an explanation that omits dissent, and avoid substituting a model summary for the proof."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Bind all five contents; the proof is a checkable term, not a narrative."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

gmeow:explainsEntry
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:FrontierExplanation ;
    rdfs:range logic:FrontierEntry ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "explains entry"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an explanation to the frontier entry it accounts for. Functional."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explainsEntry ex:rollbackEntry ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to attach an explanation to the exact frontier entry it justifies."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid attaching an explanation to the action rather than the entry: the same action under two policies is two entries with two explanations."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "One explanation per entry; the entry's derived label and the explanation must be read together."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:explanationProof
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:FrontierExplanation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "explanation proof"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The checkable derivation supporting the entry's position. Range a proof or derivation reference (stated in prose). A model-generated narrative may never occupy this position."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explanationProof ex:proofTerm ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for a checkable proof term supporting the recommendation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid binding a model-generated rationale here: advice is never authority, and a heuristic relabelled as proof is the failure this element exists to prevent."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Bind a term a checker can recompute, not one whose stated goal must be taken on trust."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:explanationEvidence
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:FrontierExplanation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "explanation evidence"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Evidence bearing on the entry's position. Range an evidence node (stated in prose). Multi-valued."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explanationEvidence ex:incidentTimeline ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for the observations and records the recommendation rests on."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid citing the proof term here; the proof is a separate element and collapsing the two hides whether anything was actually checked."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Cite evidence a reader could go and re-examine, not a summary of it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:explanationPolicy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:FrontierExplanation ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:Norm ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "explanation policy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The norm governing the entry's position. Multi-valued: where several norms bear on one action and disagree, all are surfaced."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explanationPolicy ex:fastestRestore ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to name the policy under which the recommendation holds."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid presenting a policy-relative recommendation as unconditional; under another policy the same options may tie or be incomparable."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Bind the comparison context's governing policy, so the recommendation is readable as the conditional claim it is."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:explanationCriterion
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:FrontierExplanation ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:Criterion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "explanation criterion"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A cost, risk or benefit criterion bearing on the entry, reusing the norms criterion vocabulary. Its magnitudes ground in the math: quantity spine rather than travelling as bare numbers. Multi-valued."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explanationCriterion ex:timeToRestore ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for each cost, risk or benefit criterion actually weighed in reaching the recommendation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid listing criteria that were not weighed; a decorative criterion list makes a decision look more considered than it was."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "List every criterion the comparison context ranked on, so a reader can see what was traded against what."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:explanationDissent
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:FrontierExplanation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "explanation dissent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An attributed observation that DISAGREES with the entry's position. Range an attributed observation (stated in prose). Multi-valued and required where dissent exists: suppressing it turns coexisting standpoints into a manufactured consensus, which is the failure the whole preference apparatus exists to prevent."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explanationDissent ex:onCallObjection ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to retain an attributed objection to a recommendation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid averaging dissent away into a confidence score: a recommendation that has quietly discarded the objection to it is not one an operator can properly weigh."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Keep the objection attributed to its vantage, so a competing view reads as a different standpoint rather than as noise."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:criterionMagnitude
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:range math:Quantity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "criterion magnitude"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The dimensioned magnitude a cost, risk, benefit, budget or deadline criterion carries, grounded in the math: quantity spine so it travels with its dimension rather than as a bare number. Domain a criterion or budget record (stated in prose). A quantitative claim with no dimension is an ungrounded number."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:timeToRestore gmeow:criterionMagnitude ex:ninetySeconds ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to give a decision criterion a grounded quantity rather than a bare adjective."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid a bare literal where a math: quantity is meant; an ungrounded number cannot be compared or converted."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Ground the magnitude in math: so cost, risk and benefit criteria are commensurable across explanations."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:guidanceRendering
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "guidance rendering"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The lang:-grounded textual surface of a guidance item, note, dissent or review rendering — the seam through which this slice's prose content gets a linguistic form rather than floating as an untyped literal. Range a lang: rendering (stated in prose). Domain any item carrying authored prose (stated in prose)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:reviewGuidance gmeow:guidanceRendering ex:checklistMarkdown ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to bind the human-facing rendering of a guidance set."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid letting the rendering carry content the canonical guidance lacks; a rendering is a projection, never a second source."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Ground the rendering surface in lang: so its form and denotation are explicit."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:EnactmentIsNotOccurrenceConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "an enactment is generated by an occurrence, never identical to one"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:Constraint rejecting a logic:Enactment typed as a calendar event. The schedule is the GENERATOR and the enactment is generated: identifying them makes a skipped occurrence indistinguishable from a missing run, and makes an enactment that outlives its scheduled slot unrepresentable."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:severity "Violation" ;
    logic:message "A logic:Enactment must not also be typed gmeow:Event: a schedule generates occurrences, and an occurrence generates an enactment; the three are not one thing." ;
    logic:integrity logic:einoForall .
logic:einoForall a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] ;
    logic:forall logic:einoImpl .
logic:einoImpl a logic:Formula ; logic:antecedent logic:einoGuard ; logic:consequent logic:einoCons .
logic:einoGuard a logic:Formula ; logic:relation rdf:type ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri logic:Enactment ] .
logic:einoCons a logic:Formula ; logic:not logic:einoIsEvent .
logic:einoIsEvent a logic:Formula ; logic:relation rdf:type ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri gmeow:Event ] .

gmeow:ReviewProjectionCompletenessConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "a review projection carries all eight contents and a receipt"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:Constraint rejecting a gmeow:WorkReviewProjection missing any of its eight contents or its projection receipt. Partial completeness is the failure mode that matters here: an operator view that silently omits effect status or dissent looks complete and is not, and the receipt is what discloses the collapse the view necessarily performs."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:severity "Violation" ;
    logic:message "A gmeow:WorkReviewProjection must carry all eight contents and a gmeow:reviewReceipt disclosing its preservation judgment." ;
    logic:integrity logic:rpcForall .
logic:rpcForall a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] ;
    logic:forall logic:rpcImpl .
logic:rpcImpl a logic:Formula ; logic:antecedent logic:rpcGuard ; logic:consequent logic:rpcCons .
logic:rpcGuard a logic:Formula ; logic:relation rdf:type ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri gmeow:WorkReviewProjection ] .
logic:rpcCons a logic:Formula ; logic:and logic:rpcGoal , logic:rpcLineage , logic:rpcEnactment , logic:rpcFrontier , logic:rpcApprovals , logic:rpcEffects , logic:rpcRecord , logic:rpcTimeline , logic:rpcReceipt .
logic:rpcGoal a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:reviewGoalAndRecurrence ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "goal" ] .
logic:rpcLineage a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:reviewPrescriptionLineage ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "lineage" ] .
logic:rpcEnactment a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:reviewCurrentEnactment ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "enactment" ] .
logic:rpcFrontier a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:reviewFrontier ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "frontier" ] .
logic:rpcApprovals a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:reviewApprovalsAndPending ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "approvals" ] .
logic:rpcEffects a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:reviewEffectStatus ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "effects" ] .
logic:rpcRecord a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:reviewAccumulatedRecord ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "record" ] .
logic:rpcTimeline a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:reviewTimelineRepresentation ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "timeline" ] .
logic:rpcReceipt a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:reviewReceipt ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "receipt" ] .

gmeow:ContributionAttributionConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "an explanation surfaces its dissent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:Constraint rejecting a gmeow:FrontierExplanation that carries no proof. An explanation whose supporting derivation is absent is a narrative, and a narrative presented where a proof belongs is exactly the substitution the advice-is-never-authority discipline forbids."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:severity "Violation" ;
    logic:message "A gmeow:FrontierExplanation must carry a gmeow:explanationProof; a narrative may not stand where a checkable derivation belongs." ;
    logic:integrity logic:cacForall .
logic:cacForall a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] ;
    logic:forall logic:cacImpl .
logic:cacImpl a logic:Formula ; logic:antecedent logic:cacGuard ; logic:consequent logic:cacCons .
logic:cacGuard a logic:Formula ; logic:relation rdf:type ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri gmeow:FrontierExplanation ] .
logic:cacCons a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:explanationProof ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "proof" ] .

gmeow:GuidanceVersionRecordedConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "an occurrence records the guidance version that governed it"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The logic:Constraint rejecting a logic:ContextAssembly that names no governing guidance version. Without it, 'was that occurrence done right?' can only be judged against today's guidance, which silently rewrites the past every time the guidance is edited."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:severity "Violation" ;
    logic:message "A logic:ContextAssembly must record the guidance version that governed it; otherwise a past occurrence can only be judged by present guidance." ;
    logic:integrity logic:gvrForall .
logic:gvrForall a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] ;
    logic:forall logic:gvrImpl .
logic:gvrImpl a logic:Formula ; logic:antecedent logic:gvrGuard ; logic:consequent logic:gvrCons .
logic:gvrGuard a logic:Formula ; logic:relation rdf:type ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri logic:ContextAssembly ] .
logic:gvrCons a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:assemblyGuidanceVersion ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "version" ] .

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow> ;
    rdfs:comment """The domain binding of the general prescription/enactment/commitment kernel onto continuing work.

The kernel is domain-neutral by construction: it is declared standalone in the reasoning namespace and takes no axiom edge into the gmeow: namespace, which is what lets one algebra serve a workflow, a DAG, a repeatable guide, a curriculum, a control plan and an organizational guide without privileging any of them. This slice is where the durable-work reading acquires its gmeow:-typed edges, and every bridge runs domain-specializes-kernel rather than the reverse.

It deliberately mints no second recommendation model: the derived frontier reaches the preference apparatus through gmeow:CandidateSet and gmeow:ComparisonContext, inheriting ties, positive incomparability and the no-context-free-winner discipline rather than reproducing them. It mints no second authority gate, no second budget and no second frontier for the same reason.

The operator review projection is honest about being a projection. Collapsing standpoint-indexed frontier classifications into one readable surface is a real loss, and it is disclosed on a projection receipt with an explicit preservation judgment rather than hidden — a review that presents coexisting disagreement as consensus would be the most consequential overclaim this surface could make."""@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    rdfs:label "GMEOW Work-Orchestration Module"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The work-orchestration module — the domain binding of the prescription/enactment/commitment kernel onto continuing work: the gmeow:WorkCluster spine, versioned guidance, contribution attribution, the frontier's bindings into the preference apparatus, and the operator review projection with its disclosed preservation judgment."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxConfigBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox .
